<title>JAPAN: Nomura shares continue to recover.</title>
<headline>Nomura shares continue to recover.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-03-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares of Nomura Securities Co Ltd continued to recover in the Friday afternoon session after a recent scandal involving its former directors in suspected illegal deals sent the price tumbling, brokers said.</p>
<p>By 0400 GMT, the shares had climbed 40 yen to 1,450 in turnover of 2.872 million, making Nomura the eighth most heavily traded issue on the first section of the Tokyo bourse. They had hit a year low of 1,330 on March 17.</p>
</text>
